{"findings":[{"rule_id":"NM-002","evidence":[{"kind":"note","ref":"N3","page":1,"quote":"HEAT TREATMENT NOTE :- 1) TO BE CASE HARDENED UPTO 55~60 HRC. 2) CASE DEPTH 0.8~1.2mm. 3) THREADS TO BE KEEP SOFT. 4) RETAPPING TO BE DONE AFTER SURFACE TREATMENT AT SUPPLIER END.( IF APPLICABLE )"}],"comment":"Note N3 requires threads to be kept soft and retapped after surface treatment, yet no thread feature or thread dimension exists anywhere on the drawing. This will confuse manufacturing because the shop cannot identify which features to mask during case hardening or where to cut threads; the designer should either add the missing thread dimensions or remove the thread-related instructions from N3."
    ,
    "recommended_correction": "Add the thread callout and dimensions to the drawing, or delete items 3 and 4 of note N3 if no threads are present on this pin."}]}
